index f1926ac..fd9c435 100644
--- a/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
+++ b/addons/skin.estuary/language/resource.language.en_gb/strings.po
@@ -1557,6 +1557,11 @@ msgctxt "#31748"
 msgid "Where the graphics card cannot prepare a native Dolby Vision picture in the time of a frame, even drawn the faster way and a frame ahead (an integrated one with 4K Blu-ray video and its enhancement layer), the picture can be rebuilt a little less precisely: some of its planes are scaled up with a simpler filter. In test pictures most of the pixels that change do so by the smallest step of a 12-bit picture, none by more than 16 before the last step, which can move a few pixels at edges of strong colour further. Automatic: one step at a time and only as far as the video needs to play smoothly; graphics that keep up always show the exact picture, and what is found is kept for this graphics card and build. Never: always the exact picture, even if the video stutters. Level 1, 2, 3: that level for every frame, to measure what it saves. A level changes only the frames that the renderer says it changes (with the composer of the specification, levels 1 and 2 only those that rebuild the residual of a full enhancement layer, FEL; with libplacebo's reshaping, levels 2 and 3), and a frame that it does not change is drawn at the highest level under it that changes it, or exactly, as the player information then says. While a level is set nothing that is measured is kept. A level set in advancedsettings.xml (dvstepdown) comes first. Applies from the next video."
 msgstr ""
 
+#: addons/skin.estuary/xml/DialogPlayerProcessInfo.xml
+msgctxt "#31749"
+msgid "GPU by pass"
+msgstr ""
+
 #: addons/skin.estuary/xml/Variables.xml
 #. Reason on the Dolby Vision page of the player information: native output is turned off in the settings (videoscreen.hadesdvnative)
 msgctxt "#31760"
